WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.990
Your own AI assistant, your very own Jarvis, built by you, without writing a single line of code.

2
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.910
In the last video I showed you the 7 pieces of an agent. Today you build yours.

3
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.970
And no, you don't need to know how to code.

4
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:15.470
You pick the ingredients on a page, like in a grocery store.

5
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.650
And the coding agent builds it on your machine while you watch.

6
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.470
In this video I show you the whole path on screen.

7
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:28.670
The grocery store, the file, the terminal, the files that get created, the assistant answering…

8
00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.040
and, in the end, how to keep it online 24 hours a day.

9
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.120
The path has five steps.

10
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.480
First, the grocery store:

11
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.080
you check off what you want your

12
00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.520
assistant to do and export a list.

13
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.920
Second, the terminal:

14
00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:41.560
you open Claude Code or

15
00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.900
Codex in the folder and ask it to build.

16
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.360
Third, the files:

17
00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.840
you see what was created and where

18
00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:47.900
each piece lives.

19
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:49.380
Fourth, the conversation:

20
00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:50.620
the assistant answers,

21
00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:51.820
first in the terminal,

22
00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.900
then on Telegram or WhatsApp.

23
00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.160
Fifth, the server:

24
00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.520
on a VPS, it stays on day and

25
00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:57.720
night.

26
00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.000
Each step is short.

27
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.760
The heavy lifting is done by the agent.

28
00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.440
Step one: the grocery store.

29
00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.240
It's an INTELECTO page with more

30
00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:05.720
than one hundred and forty features,

31
00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.200
taken from open projects like OpenClaw,

32
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.720
NanoBot and Hermes,

33
00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.480
organized into aisles:

34
00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:13.620
identity, security, communication,

35
00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:15.180
memory, automation.

36
00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.960
Each card explains in one sentence what

37
00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:17.720
that feature does.

38
00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.620
You click and it gets checked.

39
00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:20.900
For a first Jarvis,

40
00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:21.720
I picked eight:

41
00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.020
the personality file,

42
00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:23.920
the Telegram bot,

43
00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.810
WhatsApp, memory with search in

44
00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:27.720
SQLite, the encrypted secrets vault,

45
00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:28.880
the list of forbidden commands,

46
00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.500
scheduling and skills.

47
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:31.300
Start small.

48
00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.420
You can come back and add more later.

49
00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:34.900
The checked items go into the cart,

50
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:35.880
in the corner of the screen.

51
00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.240
Down at the bottom there's a button:

52
00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.200
export as a briefing for Claude Code.

53
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.820
One click, and it downloads a file,

54
00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:42.360
my assistant dot md.

55
00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.060
Inside it, each ingredient with what it

56
00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:46.220
does, which projects already implement it, and where

57
00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:47.540
the reference code is.

58
00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.860
But there's one important detail,

59
00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:50.920
which we found out by testing:

60
00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:52.420
this list alone isn't enough.

61
00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:53.760
It's a shopping list,

62
00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:54.840
not a recipe.

63
00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.520
The recipe is INTELECTO's construction

64
00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.320
plan, intelecto dot md,

65
00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.020
with the contracts for each piece.

66
00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:01.320
The briefing points to it,

67
00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.680
and that's what makes the build

68
00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:03.260
work.

69
00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:04.540
Step two: the terminal.

70
00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:06.380
You clone the INTELECTO repository into

71
00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.075
your projects folder and put

72
00:02:08.075 --> 00:02:09.620
my assistant dot md alongside it.

73
00:02:09.620 --> 00:02:11.520
Go into the folder and open Claude

74
00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.900
Code or Codex.

75
00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.080
Then comes the request,

76
00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.080
in one sentence: read my assistant dot

77
00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.200
md

78
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.600
and the plan in doc slash intelecto

79
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.020
dot md and build my assistant

80
00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.280
in Python, with tests.

81
00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.780
The agent reads both files,

82
00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:27.200
looks at the reference code and starts

83
00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.540
writing, piece by piece.

84
00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.260
You follow along and approve what it

85
00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:31.240
asks to run.

86
00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:32.780
You don't need to understand every line.

87
00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:34.640
You need to know what you asked for and check

88
00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:35.580
the result.

89
00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.240
Step three: the files.

90
00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.000
In the example that's in the repository,

91
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:39.860
the jarvis example,

92
00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:41.600
the agent built the core in under

93
00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:42.900
a thousand lines of Python,

94
00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.220
without installing anything.

95
00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.200
Each piece from the last video became a

96
00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:46.800
folder.

97
00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:47.900
Channels is the door:

98
00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.300
the terminal and Telegram.

99
00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.500
Agent has the loop,

100
00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.640
the heart.

101
00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:52.780
Providers is the brain,

102
00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:53.800
the language model.

103
00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.380
Memory keeps the memory in a SQLite database

104
00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:57.160
with search.

105
00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.320
Tools are the hands:

106
00:02:58.320 --> 00:02:59.720
files, commands and memory.

107
00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:01.060
And security is the vault:

108
00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:02.940
encrypted secrets and the list of forbidden

109
00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:05.040
commands, like wiping the entire disk.

110
00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:06.060
Next to the code,

111
00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.440
a workspace folder with four text

112
00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:08.840
files.

113
00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.660
This is where the assistant becomes yours.

114
00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:12.160
SOUL says who it is:

115
00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:13.160
personality,

116
00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.920
values and way of speaking.

117
00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.100
AGENTS holds the working rules.

118
00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.800
USER is about you:

119
00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.940
name, routine, preferences.

120
00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.700
And MEMORY keeps the facts it

121
00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:23.860
should always remember.

122
00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:25.240
Before each answer,

123
00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:26.940
the loop puts these four files together at the

124
00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.040
start of the conversation.

125
00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.580
Want a more direct assistant,

126
00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.120
more formal or more playful?

127
00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.900
You edit a text file.

128
00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:34.140
You don't touch the code.

129
00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.140
Step four: prove it works.

130
00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:37.420
First, the tests.

131
00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:39.380
One command runs the example's nine tests:

132
00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:40.980
memory saves,

133
00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.280
searches and forgets;

134
00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:43.860
the loop asks for a tool,

135
00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.520
runs it and answers;

136
00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:47.500
the forbidden list blocks the dangerous

137
00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:48.080
command.

138
00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:48.920
Nine pass.

139
00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:51.200
Then, a real conversation in the terminal,

140
00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.580
with a test model,

141
00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:54.340
no internet and no key.

142
00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:56.070
I say: remember that my name is

143
00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:56.200
Nei.

144
00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.040
It answers: your name is Nei.

145
00:03:58.040 --> 00:03:59.460
And the last line proves it's not a

146
00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.280
trick: the name was saved in the

147
00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:02.280
SQLite database.

148
00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.340
The memory and the loop are working

149
00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:05.140
together.

150
00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.220
To chat from your phone,

151
00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:07.300
the Telegram channel is already in the

152
00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.900
code, but it refuses to turn on

153
00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:09.520
without a token,

154
00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:10.200
on purpose.

155
00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.860
You get the token in two minutes:

156
00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:13.780
on Telegram, look for BotFather,

157
00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:16.080
send slash newbot and follow the questions.

158
00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.740
Then swap the test model for

159
00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:18.500
a real model:

160
00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:19.960
in the cloud, with a key,

161
00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:21.580
or local, with Ollama.

162
00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:23.220
The plan tells the agent to build a setup

163
00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.380
assistant that asks for the token,

164
00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:27.820
the model, the name and the personality,

165
00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:29.720
and stores the keys in the encrypted vault.

166
00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:30.740
And for WhatsApp,

167
00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.340
INTELECTO has a test base

168
00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:33.700
through the Evolution API,

169
00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:34.623
running in Docker.

170
00:04:34.623 --> 00:04:35.640
Step five: put it online.

171
00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.060
On your computer,

172
00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:38.660
the assistant sleeps when you close the

173
00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:39.200
laptop.

174
00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.160
On a VPS, a rented server,

175
00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:42.900
it stays on twenty-four hours.

176
00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.020
The path is the same:

177
00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:45.720
you log into the server through the terminal,

178
00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:46.840
clone the repository,

179
00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:48.580
open Claude Code or Codex

180
00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:49.880
and ask it to build.

181
00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:51.680
The difference is the packaging:

182
00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:53.600
for a server, INTELECTO's build page

183
00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.080
recommends Docker,

184
00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:56.380
which runs on any machine.

185
00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:58.380
On a Mac, the plan uses launchd.

186
00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:00.040
Done: you talk to your Jarvis

187
00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:01.500
from your phone, from anywhere.

188
00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:02.420
Before switching it on,

189
00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:03.510
three precautions.

190
00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:04.780
First, start small:

191
00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.720
few ingredients, tests passing,

192
00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:07.980
then grow.

193
00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:09.720
Second, secrets stay in the vault,

194
00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:11.890
never in a loose file or in the code.

195
00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:14.260
Third, an assistant that runs commands needs

196
00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:16.360
limits: the forbidden list,

197
00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:18.620
approval for dangerous actions and a single

198
00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:19.740
owner, which is you.

199
00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:22.120
INTELECTO was designed for one user,

200
00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.620
not to serve the public.

201
00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:25.180
A Jarvis with access to your machine

202
00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:26.980
is powerful, and for that very reason deserves

203
00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:27.500
care.

204
00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:28.560
To get started today:

205
00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.140
open the INTELECTO grocery store,

206
00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:32.460
check five or six ingredients and export

207
00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:32.860
the briefing.

208
00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:34.020
Clone the repository,

209
00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.920
open Claude Code or Codex

210
00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:37.640
in the folder and ask it to build with

211
00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:38.120
tests.

212
00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:40.080
Run the tests and chat with it

213
00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:40.680
in the terminal.

214
00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:43.200
Then Telegram, WhatsApp and server,

215
00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:44.100
one at a time.

216
00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:45.060
It's all open:

217
00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:47.080
the repository, the step-by-step guide

218
00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.520
and the INTELECTO course,

219
00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:49.900
on INEMA dot club.

220
00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:52.040
You choose, the agent builds,

221
00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:53.300
and the test confirms.

222
00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:54.660
See you in the next video.
